# Keep the build context small, and keep secrets out of the image.
#
# Anything listed here is either a secret that belongs in a mounted volume
# rather than baked into a layer, or bulk that would be copied in and then
# immediately shadowed by a volume mount at the same path.

# Secrets — these must arrive at runtime, never in an image layer. An image
# is copied, pushed to a registry, and pulled by anyone with read access;
# a key baked into one is a key you can no longer account for.
.env
secrets.kdbx
config/keys/
config/runtime/
config/backup.conf

# Data and state — mounted as volumes, so copying them in would be wasted
# layers hidden a moment later.
workspace/
backupvault/
state/
logs/
honestbackup-profile/
restore/

# Local noise
.git/
.gitignore
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.png
docs/*.svg
